{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.FibreCategoricalTraceForcesJones"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weak_volume_reading_admits_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.weak_volume_reading_admits_three","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L217-L231","doc":"**The weak reading does not suffice — stated, not assumed.**\n\n`exteriorSquareDim_ne_zero_iff` gives `2 ≤ N`, and `N = 3` satisfies it. The\nclass `MassTraceIsFibreCategorical` admits an instance at `N = 3` with a\nnonzero alternating weight (`weightAlt_ne_zero_at_three`, proved in the\nsibling file), so under the weak reading the alternating channel need not\nvanish and nothing forces convention D.\n\nThis is the anti-vacuity check for the distinction this file draws: the two\nreadings of condition (v) are genuinely different in consequence, not two\nphrasings of one thing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ocneanu_eq_jones_of_volume_constraint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ocneanu_eq_jones_of_volume_constraint","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L199-L215","doc":"**Convention C is excluded, with the rank sourced from the framework\naxiom.**\n\nSame re-sourcing applied to `ocneanu_eq_jones_of_fibre_categorical`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovWeights_eq_jones_of_volume_constraint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.markovWeights_eq_jones_of_volume_constraint","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L172-L197","doc":"**Convention D, with the rank sourced from the framework axiom.**\n\nIdentical in content to `markovWeights_eq_jones_of_fibre_categorical`, with\nthe hypothesis `hN : N = 2` — cited to a corpus theorem that assumes its own\n`2` and has no Lean declaration — replaced by `hvol`, the categorical volume\nconstraint of `def:quantum-observable-universe` read at the fibre.\n\nStill an implication. The premise `MassTraceIsFibreCategorical` is untouched\nand remains the open input; what this changes is that the *other* hypothesis\nis now discharged from a stated axiom of the framework instead of carried as\na citation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_three_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_three_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L161-L168","doc":"**The volume constraint excludes the colour fibre.**\n\nAt `N = 3` the exterior square is three-dimensional, so condition (v) under\nthe strong reading fails. This is the formal counterpart of the observation\nin bean `qou-n1dj` that the mass chain does not inherit the eightfold\nchapter's `N = 3` construction: the two channels are constrained by the same\naxiom to different ranks, so no re-tuning connects them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_eq_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_eq_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L143-L159","doc":"**Strong reading of condition (v): `ε` is an isomorphism `Λ²V ≅ 𝟙`.**\n\n`C(N,2) = 1` has the unique solution `N = 2`: below it the exterior square\nvanishes, above it the exterior square is at least three-dimensional and can\ncarry no non-degenerate map to a one-dimensional unit.\n\nThis is the rank statement the D-forcing chain needs, and it comes from the\nframework's own definition rather than from `thm:su2-emergence`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_ne_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_ne_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L132-L141","doc":"**Weak reading of condition (v): `ε` is onto.**\n\nIf `Λ²V → 𝟙` hits its target then `Λ²V` is nonzero, which says only `N ≥ 2`.\nRecorded to make precise how much of the volume constraint is *not* enough:\nthis reading admits every fibre of rank at least two, the colour fibre `N = 3`\nincluded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_three","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L130-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_two","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_one","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim_zero","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.exteriorSquareDim","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/VolumeConstraintForcesFibreTwo.lean#L116-L122","doc":"`dim Λ²V` for a fibre `V` of dimension `N`.\n\nStated combinatorially, exactly as `RowCapObstruction` states `dim V_λ` for\nthe three `λ ⊢ 3` channels (`weylDimSym`, `weylDimMixed`, `weylDimAlt`) — the\nsame `N`, the same idiom, so the two constraints on it compose without a\ntranslation step. ","signatureChunk":0}]}